    "rationale": "The exhaustive optimizer-free V15/R13 audit completed all 12518 start phases with 380 required-safety failures. All 291 hard-ROM cases were terminal ankle-pitch plantarflexion; their observed hard-limit excess ranged from 103 to 19803 microradians. The first V16 reserve closure raised the final pitch reserve from ten to fifteen degrees, but its complete immutable build was correctly rejected: both mirrored cmu104 starts exceeded the local support-sole planar-speed screen by 3571 micrometres per second, and the complete cmu05 validation source retained only three of four required gait cycles. No longer same-source crop exists because 05/05_01 ends at frame 598, so replacing or relabeling source data is rejected. A bounded target sweep from 10.5 to 15 degrees under the same algorithm found thirteen degrees to be the largest robust point before the cmu104 speed trajectory becomes locally marginal: it adds 52360 microradians over V15, 2.64 times the largest R13 hard-ROM excess, while cmu05 retains four bilateral cycles, cmu104 support-sole planar speed is 911241 against the 1000000 limit, and maximum protected acceleration on cmu05 is 12132000 against the 25000000 limit. This V17 identity therefore preserves every V15 source, split, crop, timing, BodySchema, USD, PD, contact, safety, ground-seating, sole-pitch and sole-roll setting. It raises the final bilateral ankle-pitch floor to minus twenty-seven degrees, providing 226893 microradians of hard-limit reserve. Each transfer is removed exactly from knee and hip pitch, preserving the summed sagittal chain command under existing bounds. Forty symmetric constrained passes spread the required transfer and prefer the adjacent knee, with hip pitch used only around exhausted knee intervals. Optimizer execution remains forbidden until fresh deterministic import, native pose, formal visual and exhaustive zero-safety dynamic evidence all pass."
